{{!-- Author: Rasel Al Mamun --}}
{{!-- CV action (FD-34, FD-146), one rule for Portfolio, the drawer, Home and Hire me: a direct link
"Download CV (PDF)" to profile.cv.href (/cv/Rasel_Al_Mamun_CV.pdf, served by Django). No `download`
attribute: the PDF opens in the browser. The visible label already names the PDF, so it is the
accessible name. `variant` is the button class (btn-primary / btn-secondary); `id` and `icon`
(download icon after the label; FD-151) are optional. Portfolio (FD-108): `lead` puts the icon before the
label, `arrow` adds → after it. --}}
{{#if profile.cv.href}}
<a class="btn {{variant}}"{{#if id}} id="{{id}}"{{/if}} href="{{profile.cv.href}}">{{#if lead}}<svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 4v11M7 11l5 5 5-5M5 20h14" /></svg> {{/if}}Download CV (PDF){{#if icon}} <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 4v11M7 11l5 5 5-5M5 20h14" /></svg>{{/if}}{{#if arrow}} <svg class="icon icon-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>{{/if}}</a>
{{/if}}
